{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Symptom\n\n`_metered_spend()` in `infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/handler.py` accumulates token spend across regions, but a single CloudWatch `ClientError` returns `None` from lines 316-318 or 329-331, discarding totals already collected from healthy regions.\n\n## Code facts from `origin/main`\n\nBoth cited paths resolve under `origin/main`: `infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/handler.py` and `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py`.\n\n`_metered_spend()` builds per-region CloudWatch queries at lines 283-315, prices token data into `total` at lines 332-337, returns `0.0` when no per-model series exists at lines 338-340, then returns `total` at line 341. The only production call site is `infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/handler.py:477`.\n\n`handler()` consumes the result at the CE-poll trigger on line 493, unavailable handling at lines 507-514, display/log text at lines 523-540, the release guard at line 562, and the attach path at line 570. The CE-poll comment at lines 491-492 says a fresh authoritative read is required when the meter is close because stale CE is costly then.\n\nExisting tests already cover full CloudWatch failure paths: listing failure returns `None` at `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py:357-367`, and data failure returns `None` at `:370-394`. They also cover successful pricing at `:397-444`, no usable series at `:869-893`, and zero-value series at `:896-925`. They do not cover a later-region failure after a healthy region contributes a partial total. The current `FakeAWS.client()` returns the same CloudWatch fake for every region at `:176-187`, so partial-region tests need a region-aware CloudWatch fake.\n\nOther `_metered_spend` references found in `origin/main`: monkeypatch helpers at `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py:249` and `:254`; direct unit calls at `:363`, `:390`, `:433`, `:889`, and `:919`.\n\n## Design\n\nUse a small result object, not a bare float: `MeteredSpend(total: float, degraded: bool, failures: tuple[MeteredFailure, ...])`, where each `MeteredFailure` stores `region` and `exception_class`. This is safer than `(total, degraded)` because line 493, line 562, log text, and tests all need the same degradation bit, while operators need failed-region details.\n\nA degraded partial is a lower bound. It may trip the fail-closed attach path when `total >= THRESHOLD_USD`. It must not release a deny policy. It must not suppress CE polling at line 493. Implement the trigger as equivalent to `due or metered is None or metered.degraded or metered.total * 5 >= THRESHOLD_USD * 4` after adapting local variable names.\n\nIf at least 1 token series contributes before or after a regional `ClientError`, return `MeteredSpend(total=<partial>, degraded=True, failures=...)`. If no token series contributes before a CloudWatch `ClientError` prevents a complete scan, keep the unavailable path by returning `None`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/handler.py` defines `MeteredSpend`.\n- [ ] `MeteredSpend.total` stores the numeric CloudWatch dollar total.\n- [ ] `MeteredSpend.degraded` is `True` when at least 1 region raises `ClientError` during the scan.\n- [ ] `MeteredSpend.failures` stores each failed region name.\n- [ ] `MeteredSpend.failures` stores each failed exception class.\n- [ ] `_metered_spend()` returns a degraded `MeteredSpend` after one region contributes token spend then a later region raises during `list_metrics`.\n- [ ] `_metered_spend()` returns a degraded `MeteredSpend` after one region contributes token spend then a later region raises during `get_metric_data`.\n- [ ] `_metered_spend()` continues scanning later regions after an earlier region raises `ClientError`.\n- [ ] When a CloudWatch `ClientError` prevents a complete scan before any token series contributes, `_metered_spend()` returns `None`.\n- [ ] Degraded-region logging includes the failed region name.\n- [ ] Degraded-region logging includes the exception class name.\n- [ ] For a degraded partial below the close threshold, the line 493 CE-poll trigger runs.\n- [ ] The line 493 CE-poll trigger still runs when `MeteredSpend.total * 5 >= THRESHOLD_USD * 4`.\n- [ ] `signal_unavailable` is `True` when `MeteredSpend.degraded` is `True`.\n- [ ] A degraded partial with `total >= THRESHOLD_USD` attaches the deny policy when it is not attached.\n- [ ] A degraded partial with `total < THRESHOLD_USD` leaves an existing deny policy attached.\n- [ ] A degraded partial with `total < THRESHOLD_USD` publishes no release notification.\n- [ ] Metered log text reports the numeric partial total when `MeteredSpend.degraded` is `True`.\n- [ ] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py` extends `FakeAWS.client()` so CloudWatch fakes can vary by `region_name`.\n- [ ] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_metered_spend_preserves_partial_total_when_later_region_listing_fails` covers the listing-failure partial.\n- [ ] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_metered_spend_preserves_partial_total_when_later_region_data_fails` covers the data-failure partial.\n- [ ] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_metered_spend_records_degraded_region_failure` covers region name logging.\n- [ ] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_metered_spend_records_degraded_region_failure` covers exception class logging.\n- [ ] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_degraded_partial_meter_triggers_ce_poll_when_below_close_threshold` covers the line 493 degraded CE poll.\n- [ ] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_degraded_partial_meter_can_attach` covers fail-closed attachment.\n- [ ] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_degraded_partial_meter_cannot_release` covers release blocking.\n- [ ] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_metered_spend_cloudwatch_failure_before_any_series_reports_unavailable` covers the `None` fallback.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py` exits 0.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify` exits 0.\n\n## Testing\n\nDuring development, run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py -k 'metered_spend or degraded_partial_meter'`. Before push, run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py`, then `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify`.\n\n## Source\n\nRaised from Gerrit change 2984 patchset 7 review feedback, then narrowed to preserve partial CloudWatch totals without weakening CE polling or release safety."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1789877841313161848,"uuid":"2e7b8c1e-3361-44b8-9f8f-7396b44eac57"}